{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And he was.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He." "<b>In Jeshurun a king.</b> The yoke of His kingship is always upon them." "<b>When the heads of the people assembled.</b> Whenever the heads of the people assemble — their gathering." "<b>The heads.</b> As in ״כִּי תִשָּׂא אֶת רֹאשׁ״ (Exodus 30) — these are worthy that I bless them. Another interpretation — <b>When they assembled.</b> When they assemble together in a single union and there is peace among them — He is their king, and not when there is discord among them (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:36.837083628Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}